# --- local state -----------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing Eve generates at runtime belongs in the repo. If one of these paths
# shows up in `git status`, something wrote into the clone that should have
# written into $EVE_HOME.
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. An unanchored pattern here would also
# match a file of the same name inside templates/ or docs/, which is source.
# Only names that are unambiguously runtime state are listed: `memory/` and
# `INDEX.md` are deliberately absent, because those names are source in this
# repo and a .gitignore that hides source is worse than one that misses a
# scratch file.
/state/
/sessions/
/mirrors/
/agents.conf
/guard-patterns
/config.local
/.eve/

# --- logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/

# --- backups and editor leftovers ------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.#*
\#*\#
*.tmp
*.eve-tmp
*.eve-preuninstall

# --- databases and secrets -------------------------------------------------
# The default engine has no index. The optional sqlite engine builds one under
# $EVE_HOME/state, but a stray db in the clone is a mistake worth catching.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --- test scratch ----------------------------------------------------------
tests/tmp/
tests/out/
.eve-test/
tmp/

# --- macOS -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.Spotlight-V100
.TemporaryItems
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.VolumeIcon.icns
.DocumentRevisions-V100
# AppleDouble resource forks. Copying this repo onto a non-HFS volume (exFAT,
# FAT32, many USB sticks and network shares) creates a ._name file beside every
# real file. They are not source, they confuse `git status`, and on some volumes
# they make git operations fail outright. Strip them with:
#   find . -name '._*' -delete
._*

# --- Windows / Linux -------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.directory
*~lock*

# --- editors and tooling ---------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
.claude/settings.local.json
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
